A Go runtime is the part of the Go system that is automatically included in your Go program and manages the program while it is running.

Think of it as:

Your Go code + Go runtime + OS

What does the Go runtime actually do?

The runtime handles things that your application shouldn't have to manage manually:

Goroutines
  - Creates and manages goroutines.
  - Schedules goroutines onto OS threads.
  - Implements the GMP scheduler (G, M, P).
Garbage Collection
  - Finds objects that are no longer reachable.
  - Reclaims heap memory.
  - Controlled partly through settings like GOGC.
